From: ZyperOS
Subject: [PATCH] evdev: a gamepad with buttons and no axes is a joystick

Without udev SDL guesses a device class from its capabilities, and only
a device with ABS_X and ABS_Y could be a joystick. The GKD Pixel 2's pad
reports buttons only (its d-pad is BTN_DPAD_* keys), so every SDL program
on plastron, which has no udev, found no pad at all.
---
--- a/src/core/linux/SDL_evdev_capabilities.c	2026-11-03 19:47:46
+++ b/src/core/linux/SDL_evdev_capabilities.c	2026-11-03 19:47:46
@@ -104,6 +104,16 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /* A gamepad with no axes at all: a handheld's built-in pad whose d-pad
+     * comes as BTN_DPAD_* keys, like the GKD Pixel 2's (ROCKNIX's singleadc
+     * joypad sets no EV_ABS with no analog channels). udev's input_id calls
+     * that a joystick too; without udev this guess is all SDL has, and
+     * without this every SDL program saw no pad on it. */
+    if (test_bit(EV_KEY, bitmask_ev) && test_bit(BTN_GAMEPAD, bitmask_key) &&
+        !test_bit(EV_ABS, bitmask_ev)) {
+        devclass |= SDL_UDEV_DEVICE_JOYSTICK; /* ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK */
+    }
+
     if (test_bit(EV_REL, bitmask_ev) &&
         test_bit(REL_X, bitmask_rel) && test_bit(REL_Y, bitmask_rel) &&
         test_bit(BTN_MOUSE, bitmask_key)) {
